    intro: "Coconut Grove is unlike any other neighborhood in Miami. The architecture ranges from historic cottages tucked under banyan trees to sleek modern waterfront builds. Exterior painting here requires a crew that can adapt to any style and deliver a high-quality finish every time. We paint all kinds of homes in the Grove. Historic wood-frame cottages need gentle pressure washing, wood repair, sanding, and multiple primer coats before the color goes on. Modern stucco homes need crack repair and UV-resistant finishes. Some Grove homes combine both. We handle it all. Color selection in Coconut Grove is more adventurous than most Miami neighborhoods. Bold front doors, tropical accent walls, deep jewel tones, and warm pastels all show up here. We love working with homeowners who want something different. We bring color samples to the house and help you find the right shade for your architecture and landscape. The Grove's tree canopy means humidity and shade are constant factors. We use paints with strong mildew resistance and primers that block tannin stains from nearby trees. The salt air from Biscayne Bay also hits properties on the eastern side of the Grove, so we recommend marine-grade products for those homes. Every Coconut Grove home has its own personality. We paint each one to match.",
